finding: The shared float64 codec does not cover sustained turning over the socket: Bun alone validates and queues real frames, and only external prediction depends on asynchronous confirmations from another clock. A socket ingress limiter that mistakenly exhausts a connection's lifetime input budget after 300 accepted tick inputs would leave the 130-tick push intact and then stall the former 600-frame socket sweep at maxAhead, below its >500 distinct PlayerInput.yaw check. The in-tab sweep never crosses that limiter; replay consumes recorded receives instead of crossing it. Keep a bounded real-socket turning check with an assertion on continued authoritative confirmation (and cover sustained ingress cheaply at its owner if shortening the browser sweep); keep the one-process replay.
